From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Configurations: add a Cygwin-aarch64 target

OpenSSL ships Cygwin targets for i386 through x86_64 but none for
aarch64, so ./Configure has nothing to select when building for
aarch64-pc-cygwin.

The platform half is identical to Cygwin-x86_64: the same Cygwin-common
inheritance and the same 64-bit bn_ops.  The architecture half comes from
mingwarm64, OpenSSL's existing AArch64-on-PE/COFF target -- asm_arch
aarch64 with the win64 perlasm scheme, which emits PE-compatible assembly
rather than the ELF form linux-aarch64 produces.

--- a/Configurations/10-main.conf
+++ b/Configurations/10-main.conf
@@ -1823,6 +1823,13 @@
         asm_arch         => 'x86_64',
         perlasm_scheme   => "mingw64",
     },
+    "Cygwin-aarch64" => {
+        inherit_from     => [ "Cygwin-common" ],
+        CC               => "gcc",
+        bn_ops           => "SIXTY_FOUR_BIT_LONG",
+        asm_arch         => 'aarch64',
+        perlasm_scheme   => "win64",
+    },
     # Backward compatibility for those using this target
     "Cygwin" => {
 	inherit_from     => [ "Cygwin-x86" ]
